  "conclusions": [
    "The observed difference is concentrated in online confirmation: new runs 43055/42920 ms versus this same-harness old run 156633 ms. Fourth-node catch-up, cold recovery and successor stages remain comparable in these finite samples.",
    "Both new runs decide only heights 4/8/12/16 in round 1, exactly the absent node's round-zero proposer turns; every healthy-proposer height decides in round 0. New run 1 additionally samples Propose then Precommit during all four absent-leader waits.",
    "Old archived deciding rounds are later at eight heights. Seven online-proposer height/round views are repeatedly observed for at least one second without publication: several have nonempty pending pools and one has an empty pool. Nonempty pending does not prove an eligible nonce prefix or body.",
    "The old executable does not expose input_availability, so an empty list of old missing_body_observations means unavailable evidence, not proof that all bodies were present. No exact internal cause is assigned to each old waiting round.",
    "Repair is exercised in both new runs: ingress reserves sixteen repair batches/thirty-two inputs; nodes 1 and 3 each report thirty-two strictly verified gossip inputs and the actual final receipts complete. Local repair counters alone are not delivery evidence. Old remote verified-gossip counts are twenty and sixteen; it still eventually finalizes all transactions through normal proposal/archive processing.",
    "New run 1 has two briefly observed missing-body follower states before prompt round-zero decisions; new run 2 samples none. Neither new run samples a sustained online-proposer wait, but bounded sampling cannot exclude every transient wait.",
    "All three runs finish thirty-four successful transactions, zero business failures, four heads at height seventeen/state version thirty-four and verified actual three-signature archived certificates."
  ],
